; SELinux policy module "kde_rdp" for the Fedora/Bazzite package.
;
; The broker is a system service (unconfined_service_t). Its PAM stack runs
; pam_selinux, which selects the account's login context (unconfined_t for an
; ordinary unconfined_u user, exactly as for SSH or a local login), but Fedora's
; policy only lets sshd and display managers enter user domains: exec of
; dbus-run-session into the desktop is otherwise denied. Both domains are
; unconfined, so this grants no new access; it only lets remote desktops run
; in the user's context instead of the service's. noatsecure, rlimitinh and
; siginh keep the environment, limits and signal state the broker prepared,
; as for sshd.
(allow unconfined_service_t unconfined_t (process (transition noatsecure rlimitinh siginh)))
